-- title:
--   Invariants in the Drinfeld coordinate ring describe `quotField`
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $k$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`, assume that the Drinfeld coordinate ring $R =$ `CoordRing q k` — the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1` — is a domain, and let $C$ be a subgroup of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Write $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` for the fraction field of $R$, let $\zeta \mapsto$ `muAction q k` $\zeta$ be the monoid homomorphism from the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity to the $k$-algebra automorphisms of $R$ obtained by scaling the two coordinates, and let `quotField q k C` be the intermediate field of $F/k$ fixed by the subgroup generated by the automorphisms of $F$ induced by the elements $(1,\zeta)$ of `hSubgroup q` for $\zeta \in C$. Two assertions are made. First, for every $b \in R$, the image of $b$ in $F$ lies in `quotField q k C` if and only if `muAction q k` $\zeta\, b = b$ for all $\zeta \in C$. Second, every $z \in$ `quotField q k C` admits $g, h \in R$, both invariant under `muAction q k` $\zeta$ for all $\zeta \in C$, with $h \neq 0$ and $z \cdot h = g$ in $F$.
--
--   This identifies the fixed field of the scalar subgroup $C$ acting on the function field of the Drinfeld curve $x y^q - x^q y = 1$ as the fraction field of the ring of $C$-invariants of its coordinate ring, in the concrete form 'an element of $R$ is fixed iff it is $C$-invariant, and every fixed element of $F$ is a quotient of invariants'. It is used to present the special fibre of a descended semistable chart as the intersection of the coordinate ring with the quotient function field, and is cited by the constructions of ring homomorphisms onto `quotField` invariants in the full-level semistable covering material.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_algebraMap_mem_quotField_iff_forall_muAction_eq_and_exists_of_mem_quotField.lean

